Original commit body from 6887d2933597d39356fa41f0fd209af2d270310f:

A Phoenix route marker (kind=function, meta.framework_role=route) also
matched the Elixir public-function library_export pattern. The concept
pass emitted LIBRARY_EXPORT (0.75) before the route-marker pass emitted
HTTP_ROUTE (0.90), and detect_entrypoints' per-symbol dedup kept the
first-emitted entry -- so every Phoenix route was filed under Library API
and the sketch's HTTP Routes section showed none of them (thc: 377 router
markers, 2 http_route entrypoints, both Express).

- detect_entrypoints keeps the most confident entry per symbol (ties to
  the earlier detector), so the kind no longer depends on detector or
  concept order.
- enrich_symbols drops the library_export concept from route-family
  markers (route / route_mount / route_include): a route registration is
  not importable API. The Go uppercase-name pattern matched "GET /x"
  markers the same way.
- The sketch's Entry Points section shares one entry budget across its
  groups instead of applying it to each (thc: 22.7k -> 7.4k chars), a
  route line names its handler instead of repeating the route, and a
  route overflow points at `hypergumbo routes`.

thc after: 240 http_route entrypoints (372 before the entrypoint cap),
0 router markers carrying library_export; HTTP Routes lists 19 routes
with handlers plus "... and 221 more".

